ctomy: a survey of US urologists</article-title><source>Contraception</source><year>2004</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>406</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15105063</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.contraception.2003.12.009</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schwingl</surname><given-names>PJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Guess</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Safety and effectiveness of vasectomy</article-title><source>Fertility and Sterility</source><year>2000</year><volume>73</volume><fpage>923</fpage><lpage>936</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10785217</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0015-0282(00)00482-9</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>